Hello distance list!

Announcing the new release of the distance sampling survey design package (dssd 0.3.0) on CRAN.

Main new features:
Improved plotting via ggplot2.
Function to aid the calculation of how much effort is required in the main survey given the pilot survey data to achieve a desired coefficient of variation. This is based on the equations in Section 2.4.2 of 'Distance Sampling: Methods and Applications'. After installing type ?calculate.effort for details on how to use.

A full list of enhancements / fixes can be found at:
https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/dssd/NEWS

